Implemented the repair in src/dotenv/parser.py only. Changed `_rest_of_line` from `r"[^
]*(?:|
|
)?"` to `r"[^
]*(?:
||
)?"`, so the alternation matches CRLF as a single unit before lone CR/LF.

Effect: after an invalid binding, error recovery now consumes the whole CRLF, so the invalid binding's original.string includes the full `
`, and the following valid binding starts at line 2 with original.string exactly `GOOD=ok
`. LF and lone-CR behavior are unchanged (each still matches its single terminator), and repeated invalid lines each consume their own complete newline. No tests, docs, other modules, or dependencies were modified.
